-- **July 18, 2003, AWA-329, physical pp. 1–3 and 12–22.** The FAA cover calls this the second submission under DOT Request No. 2 and says it fully responds to **5(c), 6, 7(c), 12, 16, 19 and 20**. It says the search for additional item 3 records continues. The index and AAT-200 response expressly list item 20 and introduce an inventory headed **“Items Provided in Response to Document Request Number 20.”** The inventory lists accident packages, re-recordings, transcripts and supporting records. Physical pp. **16, 19 and 21** name the **Washington Operations Center (ADA-30) Activity Report**. They do not provide a shared accession identifier for those entries. The 22-page object contains the cover and response/index material. It leaves the exact attached memorandum to the original July 2 request and actual media contents unverified. [AWA-329](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/34913201)
-- **July 18, 2003, AWA-820.** The separately held FBI authorization has the same calendar date and discusses records on its product list and the agreement on Moussaoui-related information. The FAA cover also cites that agreement. The calendar and subject match leave the scope of each enclosure and the order of actions open. AWA-329 does not list item **21** among the items it calls fully answered. The separate August 29 reference to a **July 16** chronology submission under item 21 stands. [FBI authorization](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/34913653) · [August 29 reply](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/34913667)
