-- **April 8, 2004, AWA-334, physical pp. 1–6.** The FAA says a staff member from the Office of the Assistant Administrator for Regions and Center Operations compiled the **Chronology of Events** while part of a group gathering information mainly for congressional hearings. It separately says staff found a document similar to the Washington Operations Center chronology with additional entries. The recovered packet puts the Chronology of Events on pp. 2–4 and has pages headed **ADA-30 Operations Center Activity Report** beginning at p. 5. Physical p. 3 pairs **0924** with **“NEADS Log shows FAA reporting AA77”**, the same attributed row previously documented in AWA-619. The transmittal supports an April 2004 disclosure route for that wording. Its provenance note does not verify the event, identify the original NEADS input or establish the July 16 packet's contents. The prior military log's **1324** row names **N334AA**, identified by the Commission with AA11. Both records remain preserved. [April transmittal](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/34913205) · [Prior chronology and military-log comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/57d7c8b17fb83a8ad089850aae49e8c3cb22469e/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-acc-event-chronology-comparison-2026-11-05/README.md)
