-## Earlier clearance and later QFR boundaries
+The August 29 DOT reply separately says its **July 16, 2003** response to Request No. 2 item 21 included a chronology involving communications to or from Secretary Mineta. The October cover references a later Commission email and describes facility files and tapes. Keep those records separate unless a shared enclosure ID, original version or receipt joins them. The separately acquired six-page Team 8 chronology had no July 16, item 21 or Mineta anchor in its available text layer. Its date heading and archive filename leave its dispatch provenance open. [August 29 reply, PDF p. 2](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/34913667) · [Prior item 21 review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/a916cdc93830ca641d72f367594e4439bbc904ce/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-item21-production-index-2026-11-05/README.md)
 
-- **May 21, 2003, AWA-839.** DOT staff send **DOTIndex1.doc** for pre-delivery review and state their belief that the proposed documents raise no executive-privilege issue. A DOJ reply asks whether the material was reviewed for executive and deliberative-process privilege and says some items, including operations logs, were unclear from the index. The archived email identifies the attachment without embedding it. The May 28 index separately names the Washington Operations Center chronology under Request No. 1 item **6**. A matching title cannot establish that the draft index, May 28 production and July 16 response used the same chronology version. [May 21 chain](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/34913681) · [May 28 index in AWA-831, physical p. 5](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/34913673)
-- **July 11 agreement and June 2004 QFR.** The released July 14 fax contains the July 11 DOJ–Commission agreement on handling specified Moussaoui-related material. The scope clause excludes PENTTBOM records DOJ determines unrelated to that investigation or prosecution. AWA-335 independently supplies a **June 8, 2004** response cover for the **May 25, 2004** questions. AWA-336 supplies the question set, beginning with closure and reopening of national airspace. They are distinct from the **May 22, 2003** answer on FAA–NORAD notification. [Agreement](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/34913669) · [June 2004 response](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7601900) · [Questions](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7601901)
